{
  "title": "Questions, pointers and connectors",
  "note": "Questions start with a question word or add -ne to the first word. Nonne expects the answer yes; num expects no. Hic, haec, hoc means this; ille, illa, illud means that. -que (and) attaches to the second word joined: senatus populusque Romanus, the senate and the Roman people. Nam, enim, ergo and tamen link sentences.",
